# Declarative Pipeline (most common)
🔹 Syntax: Simplified and structured (uses pipeline { } block)
🔹 File: Usually defined in Jenkinsfile
🔹 Purpose: Recommended for most use cases — easier to read, maintain, and validate.

pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building...'
            }
        }
        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                echo 'Testing...'
            }
        }
        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                echo 'Deploying...'
            }
        }
    }
}

✅ Best for: Teams that want readability, structure, and built-in error handling.

